    "description": "The operator's car runs the DQ250 6-speed wet dual-clutch (0D9 AWD variant) — the world's first mass-produced passenger-car DCT, designed for VAG engines up to ~350–380 Nm (dossier §3). K1 drives odd gears, K2 even, both packs submerged in oil; the J743 mechatronic unit pressurises the circuit to ~40–60 bar. Bolted to the engine's flywheel end; the AWD power take-off flange points rearward for Phase 4's Haldex driveline. Verify the gearbox code on the bellhousing label against DQ250 (a Mk7.5 would be DQ381)."
  },
